The real world is not ideal
• Our real world UW-Madison student IDs are 10 digit
numbers:
9021453190, 9033879101, 9024357190
• To define a perfect hash function we would need to define
it over the space from 0 to 10 billion
• This already exceeds the maximum size of a Java array
which is around 2 billion, so we can’t have a unique index  
