```java
// 1) build max heap
for (int i = n/2 - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
heapify(arr, n, i);
}
```  
- we start from n/2 − 1 because that is the **index of the last parent node**
- everything after that is leaves, which are trivially heaps already
- we move from the bottom up making sure each subtree is a max heap  
